      <div type="clause" n="Prol., 1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:EGu">EGu</ref> Prol., 1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="Prol., 1" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="128" ed="#liebermann"/>Ðis<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="***" target="#EGu_Prol-to-1.lnote.oe.star3"/> ærest, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> hig<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#EGu_Prol-to-1.lnote.oe.11"/> gecwædon, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> hí ænne God lufian woldon ⁊ ælcne hæþendom<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#EGu_Prol-to-1.lnote.oe.12"/> georne aworpen.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#EGu_Prol-to-1.lnote.oe.13-2"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="Prol., 1" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="128" ed="#liebermann"/>Ðæt is ærest, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> hi gecwædon, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> hí ænne God lufian woldan ⁊ ælcne hæðendom georne aworpen.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="Prol., 1" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="129" ed="#liebermann"/>Inprimis est, quod<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#EGu_Prol-to-1.lnote.oe.13"/> dixerunt, ut unum Deum diligere uelint et omni paganismo renunciare<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#EGu_Prol-to-1.lnote.oe.14"/> sedulo.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#EGu_Prol-to-1.lnote.oe.15"/></ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" n="§1" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="102" ed="#attenborough"/>Ðæt is ærest<ptr type="editorNote" n="6" target="#EGu_Prol-to-1.attnote.fn.6"/>, þæt hig gecwædon, þæt hí ænne God lufian woldon ⁊ ælcne hæþendom georne aworpen.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="2" ed="#rabin-doml"/>Pr.1 Ðæt is ærest þæt hig gecwædon: þæt hi ænne God lufian woldon and ælcne hæþendom georne aweorpen.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="129" ed="#liebermann"/>Das<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#EGu_Prol-to-1.lnote.de.1"/> ist [nämlich] erstens, dass<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#EGu_Prol-to-1.lnote.de.2"/> sie bestimmten, dass sie Einen Gott lieben wollten und jedes Heidenthum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#EGu_Prol-to-1.lnote.de.3"/> eifrig abwerfen.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#EGu_Prol-to-1.lnote.de.4"/></ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">That is [namely] first, that they determined that they would love one God and zealously cast off all heathenism.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="103" ed="#attenborough"/>In the first place they declared they would love one God, and zealously renounce all heathen practices.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="3" ed="#rabin-doml"/>Pr.1 This is foremost among those things which they agreed upon: that they would love the one God and wholeheartedly reject every heathen practice.</ab>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:VAtr_1">V Atr 1</ref>; <ref target="clause:VAtr_34">V Atr 34</ref>; <ref target="clause:IICn_5">II Cn 5</ref></note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">[Pr.1] Đæt is: Đis H</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="EGu_Prol-to-1.lnote.oe.13" n="13" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">129</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">q. d. <hi rend="italic">aus Lond; fehlt übrigen</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">q. d. from Lond; omitted in the others</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="EGu_Prol-to-1.lnote.oe.14" n="14" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">129</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">s. r. <hi rend="italic">MHkBr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">s. r. MHkBr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="EGu_Prol-to-1.lnote.oe.15" n="15" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">129</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">semper <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">semper Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="EGu_Prol-to-1.lnote.oe.star3" n="***" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">128</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">bessere mit BLd</hi> Ðæt is; <hi rend="italic">hinter der Initiale vergisst H mehrfach den Haken, der Abkürzung bedeutet</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">read with BLd Ðæt is; after the initial, H several times forgets the hook that indicates abbreviation</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="EGu_Prol-to-1.lnote.oe.11" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">128</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">hi <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">hi Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="EGu_Prol-to-1.lnote.oe.12" n="12" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">128</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-dome <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-dome Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="EGu_Prol-to-1.lnote.oe.13-2" n="13" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">128</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">geänd. in</hi> aweor. <hi rend="italic">H;</hi> aworpan <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">altered to aweor. H; aworpan Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="EGu_Prol-to-1.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">90</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Denkt man sich diesen Satz und den folgenden fort, so erschiene die Anordnung geschlossener, wäre Doppelung des ‘Erstens’ und der Heidentum-Erwähnung vermieden, und fiele die Disharmonie dieses homiletischen Satzes mit den kurzen Strafdrohungen, die folgen, fort. Vielleicht also ward diese Einleitung nur nachträglich vorangestellt. Sie ist aber archetyp und lag schon Benutzern 10. Jhs. vor: V Atr 1. 34 = VI 1. 6. = VIII 44 = IX Expl. = X 1 = I Cn 1c D = Northu 47 = 67</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">If this sentence and the following one are imagined away, the arrangement would appear more compact, the doubling of ‘first’ and of the mention of heathendom would be avoided, and the discord between this homiletic sentence and the short threats of punishment that follow would disappear. Perhaps, then, this introduction was only prefixed later. It is, however, in the archetype and was already known to users in the 10th cent.: V Atr 1. 34 = VI 1. 6. = VIII 44 = IX Expl. = X 1 = I Cn 1c D = Northu 47 = 67</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="EGu_Prol-to-1.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">90</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Nicht ‘was’; <hi rend="italic">s. Wb</hi> 217 Sp. 3 Z. 1</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Not ‘what’; <hi rend="italic">see Wb</hi> 217 col. 3 l. 1</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="EGu_Prol-to-1.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">90</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Gott 4ff.; Heidentum 8. 10</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Gott 4ff.; Heidentum 8. 10</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="EGu_Prol-to-1.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">90</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Gott 4ff.; Heidentum 8. 10</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Gott 4ff.; Heidentum 8. 10</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="EGu_Prol-to-1.attnote.fn.6" n="6" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">102</biblScope></bibl><label>ærest</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">B. <hi rend="italic">Ðis ærest</hi>. H.</seg></note>
      </div>
